                <head>No. 449.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bayard to Mr. Pendleton.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-03-09"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 9,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Pendleton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Minister, Berlin:</hi></p>
                <p>The President desires you to make known through the foreign office that the death
                    of the illustrious and venerable Emperor of Germany has deeply aroused the
                    sorrow and sympathy of the people of the United States and their Government.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
